# mutgap4_sys_tracker_unmap_stops_at_empty_block: An unmap stops at the first block that compares after it, and an emptied block compares after everything (remove_from_range; Run::compare). A full block of 240 one-page runs at the even pages 100-578 and a run at 1000 (past the full last block: a new block B1); a run at 650 splits the full block ([100..338] and [340..578] + 650); a map of [339, 651) joins the first half, and the second half, inside it at its end, is emptied and kept. An unmap of [1000, 1001) stops at the empty block, so B1 keeps its run; a map of [1001, 1002) joins B1, behind the empty block, and a probe of page 1001 maps it again (one map_memory call), since the scan stops at the empty block. Blocks only.
